Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The full attribution manifest is generated at build time by the Nuke `Pack`
target and published to docs/manual/third-party.md. See
docs/plan/01-technology-decisions.md § ADR-015 for the dependency licence audit.

Components currently in use:

  ANTLR 4 (Antlr4.Runtime, Antlr4.CodeGenerator)
    BSD-3-Clause — https://github.com/antlr/antlr4

  Microsoft.CodeAnalysis (Roslyn)
    MIT — https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn

  xunit
    Apache-2.0 — https://github.com/xunit/xunit

  System.IO.Hashing
    MIT — https://github.com/dotnet/runtime

  ZstdSharp.Port
    MIT — https://github.com/oleg-st/ZstdSharp

  K4os.Compression.LZ4
    MIT — https://github.com/MiloszKrajewski/K4os.Compression.LZ4
    Recorded explicitly per ADR-015: the package declares its licence in a file
    rather than as an SPDX expression, so it is not picked up automatically.

  Silk.NET (Silk.NET.SDL, Silk.NET.Core, Silk.NET.Maths)
    MIT — https://github.com/dotnet/Silk.NET

  SDL 2
    Zlib — https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL
    Bindings only are redistributed here; the library itself is not vendored and
    comes from the system. Recorded because a build that bundles libSDL2 carries
    the obligation, and the place to notice that is before the bundling happens.

  wgpu-native
    MIT OR Apache-2.0 — https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu-native
    Not vendored: `nuke RestoreNativeDeps` fetches the pinned, checksummed release
    named in build/native-dependencies.json into artifacts/, which git ignores.
    Recorded here rather than generated from the archive because these releases
    ship the headers and the libraries and no licence text — so unlike MoltenVK,
    there is nothing to copy out. An application that ships the library carries
    the obligation and has to include the upstream text itself.

